libopenwch — provenance and licensing
=====================================

This file records where the code and the ideas in this repository came from,
and under what terms.  It exists so that a downstream user can tell at a glance
which parts are original, which are derived, and which were consulted as
documentation only.

License summary
---------------

  Library code                LGPL-3.0-or-later     LICENSE
  (include/, lib/, ld/, mk/)                        COPYING.LGPL3
  scripts/checkpatch.pl       GPL-2.0               COPYING.GPL2
  lib/ble/wch/**              Apache-2.0            lib/ble/wch/LICENSE
  Documentation                CC0-1.0 / public domain
  (README.md, NOTICE,          (original prose, no restriction intended)
   HACKING)

`LICENSE` carries the GNU LGPL version 3 text and is the top-level entry point
for license scanners.  `COPYING.LGPL3` is the same text under its libopencm3
name.  Because the LGPL version 3 is defined as the GPL version 3 plus
additional permissions, `COPYING.GPL3` is also shipped: it is the text the LGPL
incorporates by reference.  `COPYING.GPL2` exists solely for
`scripts/checkpatch.pl`, which is GPL-2.0-only and cannot be relicensed.

Note that `lib/ble/wch/` is **not** LGPL: it is WCH's, under Apache-2.0, and it
keeps that licence.  See below.

Applications that merely link against libopenwch are unaffected by the LGPL;
the same is true of libopencm3, from which this split is inherited.

Vendored: WCH's Bluetooth LE stack (Apache-2.0)
-----------------------------------------------

`lib/ble/wch/` holds two files taken verbatim from WCH's CH583 SDK and one
licence:

  lib/ble/wch/LIBCH58xBLE.a        the Bluetooth stack, as shipped
  include/libopenwch/ble/wch/
      CH58xBLE_LIB.h               the vendor header for it, as shipped
  lib/ble/wch/LICENSE              WCH's Apache-2.0 licence text

They come from `ch583-main/EVT/EXAM/BLE/LIB/` in WCH's CH583 EVT package
(copyright (c) Nanjing Qinheng Microelectronics).  They are redistributed
unmodified under the Apache License, Version 2.0, which that SDK is released
under, and they are **not** covered by this project's LGPL.

The stack is closed source: there is no source form of `LIBCH58xBLE.a`
anywhere, and Apache-2.0 section 4(d) aside, nothing here grants a right to
reverse-engineer it.  Redistributors of this repository must keep the licence
and this notice with those files.

The wrapper code in `lib/ble/*.c` and `include/libopenwch/ble/*.h` is original
to this project and stays LGPL-3.0-or-later.  It calls the vendor API and
therefore links against the vendor archive, which is a separate work.

