Not in this repository any more
-------------------------------

Everything that is not the library now lives in its own repository:

  libopenwch-template    https://github.com/LrkSeraph/libopenwch-template
                         the application skeleton: a Makefile, a src/main.c,
                         and this library plus the companion flasher as
                         submodules.  LGPL-3.0-or-later.
  libopenwch-examples    https://github.com/LrkSeraph/libopenwch-examples
                         the worked examples, and what this library's CI
                         builds to test itself.  LGPL-3.0-or-later.
  libopenwch-tools       https://github.com/LrkSeraph/libopenwch-tools
                         wchlink, the WCH-LinkE flasher.  LGPL-3.0-or-later.

Each has its own LICENSE and NOTICE.  This repository is now only the library,
and its build needs nothing but a RISC-V toolchain: no libusb, no pkg-config,
no host tooling.

The Bluetooth LE layer is a wrapper: it declares the subset of WCH's stack API
that a peripheral needs, under this project's naming and documentation, and
forwards each call.  It contains no protocol logic and no code taken from
WCH.  See `lib/ble/README` for the boundary.

The mini libc is an independent implementation of the standard string and
memory routines, written for this project from their published semantics.  It
is not derived from newlib, from picolibc, or from any other C library, and it
carries the same LGPL-3.0-or-later terms as the rest of the library.
